        "An incident includes an injury, illness, dangerous occurrence or other event defined by company procedure. A near miss is an event that could have caused harm but did not. Reporting both helps identify patterns before someone is injured. External reporting requirements vary by jurisdiction and should be handled by the authorised organisation contact.",
        "Make the area safe if you can do so without creating further danger. Obtain emergency help where required. Notify the supervisor or safety contact promptly. Record the time, place, task, people involved, what happened and any immediate actions taken.",
        "A box falls from a shelf but misses an employee. The team should report the near miss, inspect storage arrangements and review the controls before another item falls.",
        "Do not hide minor injuries, blame people before facts are known or alter incident records. Do not move evidence unless necessary to protect people or prevent further harm.",
